g.webp 1.5x, /w/images/3/3c/Ico_stats.png 2x\"><img alt=\"￼START_WIDGET&quot;'-97ac5c498170e551END_WIDGET ￼START_WIDGET&quot;'-24df4df7c8b634e9END_WIDGET\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/3/3c/Ico_stats.png/25px-Ico_stats.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/3/3c/Ico_stats.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <details class=\"bg3wiki-uid\">\n<summary>UID</summary>\n<code class=\"bg3wiki-uid-box\">BOOK_GEN_Faction_ThievesGuildHiddenRulers</code>\n</details> <span class=\"bg3wiki-uid-link\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://bg3.norbyte.dev/search?q=name:BOOK_GEN_Faction_ThievesGuildHiddenRulers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img alt=\"https://bg3.norbyte.dev/search?q=name:BOOK_GEN_Faction_ThievesGuildHiddenRulers\" src=\"/w/images/7/70/Search_icon.svg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></a></span></span> <details class=\"bg3wiki-uid\">\n<summary>UUID</summary>\n<code class=\"bg3wiki-uid-box\">6084f8e4-20f7-426c-8a08-ec1c9ac012c7</code>\n</details> <span class=\"bg3wiki-uid-link\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://bg3.norbyte.dev/search?q=uuid:6084f8e4-20f7-426c-8a08-ec1c9ac012c7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img alt=\"https://bg3.norbyte.dev/search?q=uuid:6084f8e4-20f7-426c-8a08-ec1c9ac012c7\" src=\"/w/images/7/70/Search_icon.svg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></a></span></span></li></ul>\n</div>   \n<div style=\"clear: both;\"></div></div>\n    <h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Where_to_find\"> Where to find </span></h2>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-tooltip-box\">\n<ul><li>In the <a href=\"/wiki/Tiefling_Hideout\" title=\"Tiefling Hideout\">Tiefling Hideout</a> at <span class=\"bg3wiki-coordinates\">X:&nbsp;81&nbsp;Y:&nbsp;82</span></li>\n<li>In <a href=\"/wiki/Baldur%27s_Mouth_Basement\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Baldur's Mouth Basement\">Baldur's Mouth Basement</a> at <span class=\"bg3wiki-coordinates\">X:&nbsp;-1036&nbsp;Y:&nbsp;1011</span></li></ul>\n</div>  <h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Text\"> Text </span></h2>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-book-text\">\n<p>[The book's central argument is encapsulated in a chapter devoted to Rilsa Rael, Guild Kingpin of Little Calimshan.] \n</p><p><br>\n</p><p>In another time and another place, Rilsa Rael would be celebrated as a revolutionary. In <a href=\"/wiki/Baldur%27s_Gate\" title=\"Baldur's Gate\">Baldur's Gate</a>, in her own lifetime, she's known as a crime lord – a Kingpin of the Guild, ruling over the city-within-a-city that is the district of Little Calimshan. \n</p><p><br>\n</p><p>Rilsa's story began when she was orphaned at a young age. Her father was hanged by the <a href=\"/wiki/Flaming_Fist\" title=\"Flaming Fist\">Flaming Fist</a> for sheltering his fugitive brother. Soon after, her mother was denounced by the jealous wife of a patriar, and imprisoned in the Seatower where she perished. \n</p><p><br>\n</p><p>Alone in the world, she had learned two valuable lessons: when the law is corrupt, it is a necessity for those without the support of its enforcers to act outside it; and when the law is brutal, it is an ethical duty to act against it. \n</p><p><br>\n</p><p>Operating from within the Calim Jewel Emporium, Rilsa knows the value of everything and everyone that moves through Baldur's Gate. She controls a wide network of agents, who observe and track the exchange of goods and information as closely as any merchant or politician. But second-hand knowledge is cheap. Rilsa's real trick is to draw those with secrets to share directly into her orbit. \n</p><p><br>\n</p><p>At her Garden of Whispers, information can be shared with the Guild anonymously. Anyone with a grudge to bear or a competitor to bring low (that is to say, anyone of importance) can ensure that the whole city knows their grievance. It is said that if somebody speaks of your weak spot in the Garden at dawn, you can expect to find a knife buried in that exact spot before night falls.\n</p>\n</div>    \n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260714202752\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [vary‐revision‐sha1, no‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.049 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.051 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1357/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 32824/4194304 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 13006/4194304 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 22/200\nExpensive parser function count: 1/750\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2/5000000 bytes\nExtLoops count: 0/1000\nLua time usage: 0.011/7.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 928096/52428800 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   40.819      1 Template:MiscItemPage\n100.00%   40.819      1 -total\n 49.09%   20.038      6 Template:Icon_text\n 43.46%   17.739     15 Template:Trim\n 22.99%    9.385      2 Template:Uid\n 16.03%    6.542      1 Template:Main_only\n 13.75%    5.613      2 Template:Template_style\n 10.94%    4.467      1 Template:PageSeo\n 10.94%    4.464      2 Template:Hidden_code\n 10.52%    4.295      1 Template:Books\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key bg3wiki:pcache:idhash:12465-0!canonical and timestamp 20260714202752 and revision id 397062. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}